-- Row il-76. THE REFERENCE, as typed values: the instruments, the heading of each instruction set on the Law, the instruction of 2024, the clause as the page of 2011 prints it, the instructions that name the paragraph, the commencement as the page prints it, and the item I1.
-- Tests of the controls are in iv76-tests-controls.l4, and the assertion that FAILS on purpose (one) is in iv76-tests-red.l4.
--
-- THE QUOTATION LINES.
-- `src:N` lines are expanded mechanically from the excerpt of the Hebrew Wikisource consolidation (UNOFFICIAL, so CONSOLIDATION-ONLY) by tools/srcquote.py; N is the line number in the whole page, which the excerpt's header lists.
-- `ext:[shNNN-pPPP]` lines quote the Hebrew printed on the deposited image of Sefer HaChukim (SH) issue NNN, printed page PPP (registers/source-bundle/pages/); `ext:[shNNN-cover]` lines quote the cover of the issue. They are official instruments.
-- A quotation line that says "joined" is the printed lines of the line above it, joined with one space, so that a typed string that runs across a line break is on a quotation line whole.
-- Every Hebrew string typed below is a stretch of the quotation line above it, and tools/hebcheck.py checks that each Hebrew run of this module is in the excerpt or on an ext: line.
-- Where a quotation mark is printed around words, the ext: line types it as the Hebrew gershayim. A footnote reference number printed beside a heading is left out of the quotation line.
-- Nothing is quoted from memory. Every date, number and section below is on a quotation line or in NOTES.md.

§ `References`

